---
import BaseLayout from "@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Hero from "@/components/Hero.astro";
import Section from "@/components/Section.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title="Corsarium | Home" description="An open educational platform for learning bioinformatics, with a focus on structural bioinformatics.">
    <Hero />

    <Section tone="alt" labelledby="learn-heading">
        <h2 id="learn-heading" class="font-display text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-foreground sm:text-4xl">
            What you'll learn
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-4 max-w-2xl text-lg text-foreground-muted">
            Corsarium will cover structural bioinformatics from the foundations to the analyses and tools used in research.
        </p>

        <ul class="mt-10 grid gap-6 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3">
            <li class="rounded-xl bg-surface p-6">
                <h3 class="font-display text-xl font-semibold text-foreground">Foundations</h3>
                <p class="mt-3 text-foreground-muted">
                    Molecular biology and protein structure, explained from the beginning.
                </p>
            </li>
            <li class="rounded-xl bg-surface p-6">
                <h3 class="font-display text-xl font-semibold text-foreground">Sequence analysis</h3>
                <p class="mt-3 text-foreground-muted">
                    How biological sequences are compared and interpreted.
                </p>
            </li>
            <li class="rounded-xl bg-surface p-6">
                <h3 class="font-display text-xl font-semibold text-foreground">Structural databases</h3>
                <p class="mt-3 text-foreground-muted">
                    Where experimental and predicted structures come from, such as the PDB and AlphaFold.
                </p>
            </li>
            <li class="rounded-xl bg-surface p-6">
                <h3 class="font-display text-xl font-semibold text-foreground">Molecular visualization</h3>
                <p class="mt-3 text-foreground-muted">
                    How to look at molecular structures and read what they show.
                </p>
            </li>
            <li class="rounded-xl bg-surface p-6">
                <h3 class="font-display text-xl font-semibold text-foreground">Simulation and docking</h3>
                <p class="mt-3 text-foreground-muted">
                    How molecules move and interact, studied with molecular dynamics, docking and force fields.
                </p>
            </li>
            <li class="rounded-xl bg-surface p-6">
                <h3 class="font-display text-xl font-semibold text-foreground">Tools and workflows</h3>
                <p class="mt-3 text-foreground-muted">
                    The command line, scientific programming and reproducible workflows behind the analyses.
                </p>
            </li>
        </ul>
    </Section>

    <Section labelledby="how-heading">
        <h2 id="how-heading" class="font-display text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-foreground sm:text-4xl">
            How it works
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-4 max-w-2xl text-lg text-foreground-muted">
            Learning paths will be organized from first steps to advanced topics, so you can start where you are.
        </p>

        <ol class="mt-10 grid gap-8 md:grid-cols-3">
            <li>
                <span aria-hidden="true" class="font-display text-4xl font-semibold text-accent">1</span>
                <h3 class="mt-2 font-display text-xl font-semibold text-foreground">Choose a path</h3>
                <p class="mt-3 text-foreground-muted">
                    Begin from zero, or jump in at the topic you want to learn or review.
                </p>
            </li>
            <li>
                <span aria-hidden="true" class="font-display text-4xl font-semibold text-accent">2</span>
                <h3 class="mt-2 font-display text-xl font-semibold text-foreground">Learn step by step</h3>
                <p class="mt-3 text-foreground-muted">
                    Each lesson builds on the previous one, introducing concepts before the tools that use them.
                </p>
            </li>
            <li>
                <span aria-hidden="true" class="font-display text-4xl font-semibold text-accent">3</span>
                <h3 class="mt-2 font-display text-xl font-semibold text-foreground">Apply the tools</h3>
                <p class="mt-3 text-foreground-muted">
                    Work through different analyses and the tools used to run them.
                </p>
            </li>
        </ol>
    </Section>

    <Section tone="alt" labelledby="audience-heading">
        <h2 id="audience-heading" class="font-display text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-foreground sm:text-4xl">
            Who it's for
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-4 max-w-2xl text-lg text-foreground-muted">
            Corsarium will guide you through structural bioinformatics, whether you are just starting out or already working in the field.
        </p>

        <ul class="mt-10 grid gap-6 md:grid-cols-2">
            <li class="rounded-xl bg-surface p-6">
                <h3 class="font-display text-xl font-semibold text-foreground">New to the field</h3>
                <p class="mt-3 text-foreground-muted">
                    Start with no prior knowledge. Corsarium will guide you step by step, from the first concepts to the different analyses and tools researchers use.
                </p>
            </li>
            <li class="rounded-xl bg-surface p-6">
                <h3 class="font-display text-xl font-semibold text-foreground">Already working in the field</h3>
                <p class="mt-3 text-foreground-muted">
                    Learn new analyses and tools, or cross-check what you already know against a clear, structured guide.
                </p>
            </li>
        </ul>
    </Section>

    <Section labelledby="open-heading">
        <h2 id="open-heading" class="font-display text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-foreground sm:text-4xl">
            Open and free
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-4 max-w-2xl text-lg text-foreground-muted">
            Corsarium is open source and free to use. The code is public on GitHub under the MIT License, and you can follow the project, report problems or contribute.
        </p>

        <a
            href="https://github.com/GuilleCF/corsarium"
            class="mt-8 inline-flex items-center rounded-full bg-accent px-6 py-3 font-medium text-background transition-colors duration-200 hover:bg-accent-hover focus-visible:outline-hidden focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-accent focus-visible:ring-offset-2 focus-visible:ring-offset-background"
        >
            View the source code
        </a>
    </Section>
</BaseLayout>
